---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'One Agent or a Team of Agents?';
const description =
	'It feels obvious that a team of AI agents should beat a single one. Three recent studies say: usually not — and the exceptions are where it gets interesting.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
	<Fragment slot="head">
		<style>
			:root {
				--ink: #16202a;
				--muted: #596774;
				--line: #d8e0e6;
				--paper: #ffffff;
				--wash: #f5f7f7;
				--blue: #2a78d6;
				--aqua: #1baf7a;
				--gold: #a27517;
				--red: #d03b3b;
				--green: #23715b;
			}

			body {
				background: #ffffff;
				color: var(--ink);
			}

			main {
				width: 100%;
				max-width: none;
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
			}

			.wrap {
				width: min(100% - 2rem, 1180px);
				margin: 0 auto;
			}

			section {
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
			}

			.hero {
				padding: 4.5rem 0 3.5rem;
				background: linear-gradient(180deg, #f7faf9 0%, #ffffff 78%);
			}

			.kicker,
			.eyebrow {
				margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
				color: var(--green);
				font-size: 1rem;
				font-weight: 700;
				text-transform: uppercase;
			}

			h1,
			h2,
			h3,
			p {
				margin: 0;
			}

			h1 {
				max-width: 840px;
				font-size: clamp(2.45rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
				line-height: 1.02;
			}

			h2 {
				max-width: 940px;
				font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.4vw, 2.9rem);
				line-height: 1.08;
			}

			h3 {
				font-size: 1.22rem;
				line-height: 1.3;
			}

			.lede {
				max-width: 780px;
				margin-top: 1.4rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.35rem);
				line-height: 1.58;
			}

			.thesis {
				max-width: 820px;
				margin-top: 1.6rem;
				padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
				border-left: 5px solid var(--green);
				background: #eef7f3;
				color: #173d32;
				font-size: 1.16rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
			}

			.tldr {
				max-width: 820px;
				margin-top: 1.5rem;
				padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: var(--paper);
			}

			.tldr .eyebrow {
				margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
			}

			.tldr ul {
				display: grid;
				gap: 0.6rem;
				margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
				padding-left: 1.25rem;
			}

			.tldr li {
				font-size: 1.15rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
			}

			.nav {
				position: sticky;
				top: 3.35rem;
				z-index: 4;
				background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.93);
				border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
				backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
			}

			.nav .wrap {
				display: flex;
				gap: 0.45rem;
				overflow-x: auto;
				padding: 0.7rem 0;
			}

			.nav a {
				flex: 0 0 auto;
				padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
				border-radius: 999px;
				color: var(--ink);
				font-size: 1.02rem;
				line-height: 1;
				text-decoration: none;
			}

			.nav a:hover {
				background: #edf3f8;
				color: var(--blue);
			}

			.block {
				padding: 4.2rem 0;
				scroll-margin-top: 7rem;
			}

			.block.alt {
				background: var(--wash);
			}

			.section-head {
				display: grid;
				gap: 0.9rem;
				margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
			}

			.section-head p {
				max-width: 820px;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 1.16rem;
				line-height: 1.65;
			}

			.prose {
				display: grid;
				gap: 1rem;
				max-width: 920px;
			}

			.prose p {
				color: var(--ink);
				font-size: 1.18rem;
				line-height: 1.7;
			}

			.takeaway {
				max-width: 920px;
				margin-top: 1.3rem;
				padding: 1.05rem 1.2rem;
				border-left: 5px solid var(--gold);
				background: #fff8ea;
				color: #4f3b11;
				font-size: 1.16rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
			}

			/* figures & charts */
			.fig {
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
				padding: 1.2rem 1.25rem 1rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: var(--paper);
			}

			.fig .fig-title {
				font-size: 1.18rem;
				font-weight: 650;
				color: var(--ink);
			}

			.fig .fig-sub {
				margin-top: 0.25rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				line-height: 1.5;
			}

			.fig .fig-how {
				margin-top: 0.6rem;
				padding: 0.6rem 0.85rem;
				border-radius: 8px;
				background: #eef4fc;
				color: #1d4977;
				font-size: 1.02rem;
				line-height: 1.55;
			}

			.chart {
				width: 100%;
				height: auto;
				display: block;
				margin-top: 0.6rem;
				font-family: inherit;
			}

			figure {
				margin: 0;
			}

			figcaption {
				margin-top: 0.7rem;
				padding-top: 0.6rem;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 1.05rem;
				line-height: 1.55;
			}

			/* stat tiles */
			.tiles {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
				gap: 1rem;
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
			}

			.tile {
				padding: 1.05rem 1.15rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: var(--paper);
			}

			.tile .val {
				color: var(--ink);
				font-size: 1.85rem;
				font-weight: 650;
				line-height: 1.15;
			}

			.tile .lab {
				margin-top: 0.45rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 1rem;
				line-height: 1.5;
			}

			/* card grids (defects, topologies, sources) */
			.cards {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
				gap: 1rem;
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
			}

			.topos {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
				gap: 1rem;
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
			}

			.card {
				padding: 1.05rem 1.1rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: var(--paper);
			}

			.card h3 {
				margin-bottom: 0.45rem;
				font-size: 1.18rem;
			}

			.card p {
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 1.08rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
			}

			.card .mini {
				width: 100%;
				height: auto;
				margin-bottom: 0.55rem;
			}

			.card .quote {
				margin-top: 0.55rem;
				padding-left: 0.7rem;
				border-left: 3px solid var(--line);
				font-style: italic;
			}

			/* DPI theory box */
			.dpi {
				display: grid;
				gap: 0.6rem;
				max-width: 920px;
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
				padding: 1.2rem 1.3rem;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 12px;
				background: var(--paper);
			}

			.dpi .legend {
				margin-top: 1rem;
				padding-top: 0.9rem;
				border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 1rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
			}

			.dpi .legend strong {
				color: var(--ink);
			}

			.dpi .eq {
				margin-top: 0.7rem;
				color: var(--ink);
				font-size: 1.22rem;
				font-weight: 700;
			}

			.dpi .gloss {
				margin-top: 0.6rem;
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 1.08rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
			}

			.guide {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
				gap: 1rem;
				margin: 1.8rem 0;
			}

			.guide .card ul {
				display: grid;
				gap: 0.55rem;
				margin: 0.55rem 0 0;
				padding-left: 1.15rem;
			}

			.guide .card li {
				color: var(--muted);
				font-size: 1.08rem;
				line-height: 1.6;
			}

			/* tables */
			.table-wrap {
				width: 100%;
				overflow-x: auto;
				border: 1px solid var(--line);
				border-radius: 8px;
				background: #ffffff;
				margin-top: 1.4rem;
			}

			table {
				width: 100%;
				min-width: 680px;
				border-collapse: collapse;
				font-size: 1rem;
				line-height: 1.45;
			}

			th,
			td {
				padding: 0.85rem;
				border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
				text-align: left;
				vertical-align: top;
			}

			th {
				background: #eef3f0;
				color: #25362f;
				font-size: 0.9rem;
				text-transform: uppercase;
			}

			tr:last-child td {
				border-bottom: 0;
			}

			.closing {
				background: #10251f;
				color: #ffffff;
			}

			.closing h2,
			.closing h3 {
				color: #ffffff;
			}

			.closing .section-head p,
			.closing .card p {
				color: #dce8e3;
			}

			.closing .card {
				border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22);
				background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
			}

			.closing a {
				color: #aee4d1;
			}

			a {
				text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
			}

			@media (max-width: 980px) {
				.tiles,
				.cards {
					grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
				}

				.topos {
					grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
				}
			}

			@media (max-width: 680px) {
				.hero,
				.block {
					padding: 3rem 0;
				}

				.tiles,
				.cards,
				.topos {
					grid-template-columns: 1fr;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</Fragment>
	<main>
			<section class="hero" id="top">
				<div class="wrap">
					<p class="kicker">AI agents · three studies, one story · ~10 min read</p>
					<h1>One agent or a team of agents? The answer isn't what you'd guess.</h1>
					<p class="lede">
						Give an LLM a task and it handles the whole thing itself — plans,
						writes, checks, fixes — in one long session. Splitting a complete
						job across specialized agents — a planner, a coder, a tester, a
						critic — feels like it should work better than one agent, and that
						intuition powers a lot of AI products right now. But three recent
						studies put it to the test, and the honest answer is: only
						sometimes. The interesting part is finding out exactly <em>when</em>.
					</p>
					<p class="thesis">
						Quick vocabulary check. A <strong>single-agent system (SAS)</strong>
						is one model doing the whole job in one long session. A
						<strong>multi-agent system (MAS)</strong> is several agents —
						planner, coder, tester, critic — splitting that job and passing
						messages to each other. This post is about figuring out when
						splitting the job actually pays off.
					</p>
					<div class="tldr">
						<p class="eyebrow">TL;DR for the impatient</p>
						<ul>
							<li>
								<strong>The team advantage is evaporating.</strong> As base models
								get better, agent teams win by less — often by nothing — while
								still burning 5–200× more tokens.
							</li>
							<li>
								<strong>Teams only pay off when the task splits.</strong>
								Parallelizable work gained up to +80%; sequential planning got
								<em>worse</em> under every team layout tested.
							</li>
							<li>
								<strong>Match the compute and most wins vanish.</strong> Give one
								agent the same thinking budget as the whole team, and the solo
								agent usually comes out on top.
							</li>
							<li>
								<strong>The winning move is dynamic.</strong> Try solo first,
								verify, escalate only on failure — the best accuracy in the study
								at ~12% of the team's cost.
							</li>
						</ul>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<nav class="nav" aria-label="page sections">
				<div class="wrap">
					<a href="#hybrid">The price of teamwork</a>
					<a href="#scaling">Does team structure matter?</a>
					<a href="#budget">The fair fight</a>
					<a href="#agenda">What to build instead</a>
					<a href="#sources">The papers</a>
				</div>
			</nav>

			<!-- ============ PAPER 1: Gao et al. ============ -->
			<section class="block alt" id="hybrid">
				<div class="wrap">
					<div class="section-head">
						<p class="eyebrow">Part 1 · The price of teamwork</p>
						<h2>AI teams used to win big. The gap is almost gone.</h2>
						<p>
							The first study, from a team at the University of Illinois (Gao
							et al., 2025), runs 9 popular multi-agent frameworks against a
							plain single agent on the same tasks. Most of these frameworks
							were designed back when base models needed the extra hands —
							planning was brittle, tool calls failed, context windows were
							short. A lot of that isn't true anymore, which raises the obvious
							question the paper goes after: are these frameworks still earning
							their keep? To find out, they reran the original benchmarks — same
							framework, same dataset — on a current model.
						</p>
					</div>

					<div class="fig">
						<figure>
							<div class="fig-title">Figure 1 · The MAS advantage is evaporating as base models improve</div>
							<div class="fig-sub">Same framework, same dataset — re-run with a modern base model. The gap that motivated multi-agent designs shrinks from +8–16 points to under 3.</div>
							<div class="fig-how"><strong>How to read it:</strong> each row is two dots — blue for solo, green for team — and the bar between them is the team's lead. Watch that bar collapse in every "Gemini-2.0-Flash" row.</div>
