								<circle cx="45" cy="92" r="11" fill="#1baf7a"/>
								<circle cx="100" cy="90" r="11" fill="#1baf7a"/>
								<circle cx="155" cy="92" r="11" fill="#1baf7a"/>
								<text x="100" y="116" font-size="12.5" fill="#596774" text-anchor="middle">star + lateral exchange</text>
							</svg>
							<h3>Hybrid</h3>
							<p>A manager, plus some hallway conversation between teammates.</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="prose">
						<p>
							Run the same task through all five team layouts, and here's the
							surprising part: which one wins has almost nothing to do with the
							layout itself. It depends entirely on what kind of task you gave
							it:
						</p>
					</div>

